   "title": "README: H3 LongTake Image -> Video",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 LongTake: Image -> Video (+ Refine)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s each), with one clip in VRAM/RAM at a time: 30 s or 5 minutes cost the same memory, only time (~3.2 min per clip at 0.5 MP on 16 GB). Every clip lands in `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/` with the audio generated by H3; you can stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`) and assemble at the end.\n\n**1. Image -> Video**\n- `start_image`: the first frame (keyframe on frame 0). Optional `end_image` = last frame.\n- `prompts`: **one block per clip**, separated by a line with `---`. Block *i* drives clip *i* (0-5 s, 5-10 s, ...); the last one repeats. Describe the action of each stretch; the character is fixed by the picture (and the references), no need to repeat it.\n- Model: **fl2va + Turbo fl2v** without references, or **ref2va + Turbo ref2v** with `identity_reference` (start_image as <Picture 1> in every clip) and/or `face_image` (close-up as <Picture 2>). Measured over 30 s: without a reference the face becomes another person within 20 s (ArcFace 0.27); with the face 0.60.\n- Flow: `dry_run=true` -> check the plan and the clip table -> prompts; then `max_clips=1` for the first clip; then `max_clips=0`.\n\n**2. Refine (second pass, muted: Ctrl+M)**: video \"hires fix\", clip by clip, 0.5 MP -> 1.0 MP. With `upscale = latent_model` (default; needs the Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler pack and its model) it enlarges the latent without the VAE round trip: measured a third faster and much sharper faces at denoise 0.4 / 4 steps. With `ref_image_1` + `face_image` it puts the picture's face back on the whole video. Output in `<project_name>/hr` (in the Stitch: `project_name = name/hr`).\n\n**3. Stitch (muted: Ctrl+M)**: assembles the chunks without re-encoding, with the generated audio. Connect its `project_dir` from Image -> Video, the Refine or FaceRefine.\n\nTips: 0.5 MP for the first pass on 16 GB; `context_frames=5` and `seam_match=color` are the measured defaults."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 LongTake: Image -> Video (+ Refine)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip (124 frames = 5.2 s each), with one clip in VRAM/RAM at a time: 30 s or 5 minutes cost the same memory, only time (~3.2 min per clip at 0.5 MP on 16 GB). Every clip lands in `output/h3_longtake/<project_name>/` with the audio generated by H3; you can stop, resume (`mode=continue`), redo one clip (`redo_one`) and assemble at the end.\n\n**1. Image -> Video**\n- `start_image`: the first frame (keyframe on frame 0). Optional `end_image` = last frame.\n- `prompts`: **one block per clip**, separated by a line with `---`. Block *i* drives clip *i* (0-5 s, 5-10 s, ...); the last one repeats. Describe the action of each stretch; the character is fixed by the picture (and the references), no need to repeat it.\n- Model: **fl2va + Turbo fl2v** without references, or **ref2va + Turbo ref2v** with `identity_reference` (start_image as <Picture 1> in every clip) and/or `face_image` (close-up as <Picture 2>). Measured over 30 s: without a reference the face becomes another person within 20 s (ArcFace 0.27); with the face 0.60.\n- Flow: `dry_run=true` -> check the plan and the clip table -> prompts; then `max_clips=1` for the first clip; then `max_clips=0`.\n\n**2. Refine (second pass, muted: Ctrl+M)**: video \"hires fix\", clip by clip, 0.5 MP -> 1.0 MP. With `upscale = latent_model` (default; needs the Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler pack and its model) it enlarges the latent without the VAE round trip: measured a third faster and much sharper faces at denoise 0.4 / 4 steps. With `ref_image_1` + `face_image` it puts the picture's face back on the whole video. Output in `<project_name>/hr` (in the Stitch: `project_name = name/hr`).\n\n**3. Stitch (muted: Ctrl+M)**: assembles the chunks without re-encoding, with the generated audio. Connect its `project_dir` from Image -> Video, the Refine or FaceRefine.\n\nTips: 0.5 MP for the first pass on 16 GB; `context_frames=5` and `seam_match=color` are the measured defaults."
   },
