   "title": "FaceRefine in the take",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Automatic FaceRefine (small faces)\n\n**H3 LongTake FaceRefine** takes the project and, clip by clip, regenerates the face only where it is **small** (wide shot): clips whose median face is above `max_face_px` (150, measured with FaceRefine's tracker) are copied as they are. It writes `<project>/fr`, which the Stitch assembles with the audio.\n\n**Needs** [ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine](https://github.com/Carasibana/ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine) (Carasibana). The bypassed \"Placeholder\" node only makes it show up among the Manager's **missing nodes** when it is not installed.\n\n**Measured** (15 s take, wide closing shot, 0.55 MP): face identity in the wide shot 0.25-0.33 -> 0.64-0.66, face steady on the head (< 1% of the side), flicker +2%, 3.5 min. At 1 MP: 0.44 -> 0.61, 4.8 min.\n\n**Knobs**: `denoise` 0.25-0.35; `description` = the subject's hair and outfit; FaceRefine's model must be the **ref2va** (even if the render uses fl2va). To check the clips first, mute (Ctrl+M) FaceRefine and the Stitch: clips already done are not regenerated."
   ]
  }
